\subsection{\code{BaseRStripchartLayerProcessor$group_selectors()}}{
  The marks one group was drawn into

Built rather than searched for. \code{find_graphics_plot_grob()} answers
with the first \code{points} grob of the plot, and a stripchart draws one
per group, so a search would give every layer the first group's marks.
The names are \code{graphics-plot-{plot}-points-{group}}, measured against a
real \code{gridSVG} export, and every emitted selector was then resolved in
Chromium against a rendering of a three-group chart: 5, 4 and 2
elements, one per observation.
